# Host list template: cp hosts.conf.example hosts.conf then edit (hosts.conf stays out of git)
#
# Format (| separated, one node per line):
#   name|address|reality_sni|reality_dest|reality_port|hy2_port|ss_port
#
#   - name        : node id (lowercase letters/digits/hyphens), also out/ dir name
#   - address     : VPS public IP
#   - reality_sni : Reality masquerade domain (client TLS server_name, must be a real site)
#   - reality_dest: fallback target (shown on port 443 with no valid client), usually same as sni
#   - reality_port: VLESS+Reality listen port (TCP)
#   - hy2_port    : Hysteria2 listen port (UDP); same 443 as reality_port is fine (different stacks)
#   - ss_port     : Shadowsocks 2022 listen port (TCP+UDP)
#
# Tip: use different SNI per node (e.g. microsoft / apple) for anti-censorship diversity.
# After changing ports/SNI re-run ./scripts/gen.sh, re-upload server.json and restart the service.

node-a|1.2.3.4|www.microsoft.com|www.microsoft.com|443|443|8388
node-b|5.6.7.8|www.apple.com|www.apple.com|443|443|8388
